c9eab1ae (1993 1792566984317 "guenchi" (("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f313p1") (src . "working, tools: structural drafts: a file created or deleted as a writer's draft, committed in one batch\n\nA draft can now create a file or delete one, beside the block drafts that change a source:\nworking-new and working-delete entries in the writer's structural area, each with its own\nversion and the cut it was written at. edit-sync turns a file added under an exported directory\ninto a new-file draft and a recorded file gone from disk into a delete draft, refusing a path\noutside the store route's domain (dot-named, not text, a mode other than 100644, a case\ncollision in the resulting tree) and refusing when a live structural draft of the writer is not\naccounted for by the export it syncs (the remedy is a fresh export); the overlay, dump and\nrestore, the freeze and the commit carry both kinds. The commit turns them into the holder's\ninsert with its pieces, by the construction import-git now shares, and the deletions, in one\nbatch with the block drafts; its answer maps each provisional id to the holder it created, and a\nreplay of the same request recovers that mapping. A file added this way is not shown by the\nreaders of the working view other than the export (outline, context, eval --working).\n") (parent . root) (ord . 435))))
